# layer-contract-conformance-b is a shard driver: it execs the sibling layer-contract-conformance/run.sh --group b, and declares the parent's paths but TWO.
# .githooks/: only the parent's FULL run opens the hook; this shard passes with it absent (BL-1098). And
# the parent keys +CLAUDE.md, which only the parent's FULL control run opens. Every run this shard makes is `--arms`
# selected, and a FIFO probe (CLAUDE.md replaced by a FIFO) found a selected run on the unmutated contract never opens
# it, while the full run on the same tree did.
# The validator walks the whole distribution tree and renders its arm map via render-invariant-index.sh --arm-lines <src>, which needs no root marker.
# A complete sandbox trace of this shard opens no path under templates/, patterns/ or .claude/rules/.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/
# reason: core/ is walked by content -- the validator the parent run.sh runs (layer-contract-conformance/run.sh, in process) finds every core/*.sh and derives core/*/, scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh:2476 and :3327.
core/
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
core/fixtures/*/inputs.decl
